Subject: [PATCH v2 2/2] zib: Patch review workflow - Archiving mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: lknvxszrtysqspqrwnmmurkkkzmzwutt

Archiving closes a message for everyone by moving its file into
maildir/archive/. The document did not say who may do that, and its
rule that a message's file is never renamed would forbid the move.

Only the moderator archives. Contributors keep the guarantee the
moderator relies on, that their commits only add messages, and they
still answer everything in their inbox, so nothing they owe a reply
disappears unanswered. The moderator's move keeps the file's content
and name, and only its directory changes, so the list stays immutable
in the sense that matters: no message is ever edited.
